    "b-sks-rc-events-intro": {
      "id": "b-sks-rc-events-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "EVENT — A target climbs through scored submissions; once it hits 100 % it is good. The stored event table exists for the exceptions and nothing else: one row per event, keyed to the target by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", append-only, ordered by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "created_at",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Two kinds are defined — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "regression",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", a previously good state broken by something outside the worker's control, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "note",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", a freeform human annotation — but only "
        },
        {
          "insert": "note",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows are written today: the regression pathway was retired on 2026-09-02. A run whose diff failed to integrate carries that on its own "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "conflicted",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration_detail",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with the conflict paths), where the next worker sees it on the card; reconciliation records nothing here. Good news is never an event: it is visible in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target_status",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and the submissions themselves, and per-run echo rows do not exist. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event_ref",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows name the worker run, epoch, PR, or commit involved. Run telemetry (queue, retry, claim, heartbeat, epoch open and close) stays in run state; it is not part of the knowledge system and never becomes a row here."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
